, Burmese, Nepali, Pakistani, and Sri Lankan cuisines. It is present in the closely related Caribbean cuisines, as well as in Lunigiana cuisines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chickpea-flour"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chickpea_flour"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]],["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Panella","dish/panella"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Dried lime","ingredient/dried-lime"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ground turkey","ingredient/ground-turkey"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Meatball","ingredient/meatball"],["Onions","ingredient/onions"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5e/Gram_flour_AvL.jpg/500px-Gram_flour_AvL.jpg","w":500,"h":331,"by":"AlexanderVanLoon","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gram_flour_AvL.jpg"}},"ingredient/chayote":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/chayote","n":"Chayote","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Chayote, also known as christophine, mirliton, güisquil, and choko, is an edible plant belonging to the gourd family, Cucurbitaceae. This fruit was first cultivated in Mesoamerica between southern Mexico and Honduras, with the most genetic diversity available in both Mexico and Guatemala. It is one among dozens of foods introduced to the Old World during the Columbian Exchange, particularly the galleon trades in Spanish Manila. At that time, the plant spread to other parts of the Americas, ultimately causing it to be integrated into the cuisine of many Latin American nations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chayote"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chayote"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Mie gomak","dish/mie-gomak"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Andaliman","ingredient/andaliman"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"]]}]},"dish/pastini":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pastini","n":"Pastini","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pastini (formerly Pastini Pastaria) is a chain of Italian-American restaurants in the U.S. state of Oregon. There were eight restaurants in 2017. In 2018, the company was among the largest in Oregon owned by women, with approximately 300 employees, according to Portland Business Journal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pastini"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastini"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and cour